<title>UK: Imperial Tobacco defies FTSE gloom.</title>
<headline>Imperial Tobacco defies FTSE gloom.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Tobacco Plc defied the overall weak tone in the UK equity market on Wednesday amid renewed takeover speculation, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 2p at 380-1/2 by 0917 GMT in volume of 692,481 shares, even as the FTSE 100 was down 30.5 points with only eight of its members showing an increase.  </p>
<p>&quot;There is comment in the papers again that B.A.T might be looking at Imperial and that is the main reason the stock is holding up,&quot; said one senior sales trader.</p>
<p>B.A.T shares were up 1-1/2p at 489-1/2.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
